  "question": {
    "text": "The value of $\\mathrm{n}$ for which $\\frac{\\mathrm{x}^{\\mathrm{n}+1}+\\mathrm{y}^{\\mathrm{n}+1}}{\\mathrm{x}^{\\mathrm{n}}+\\mathrm{y}^{\\mathrm{n}}}$ is the geometric mean of $\\mathrm{x}$ and $\\mathrm{y}$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{n}=-\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{n}=\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{n}=1$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{n}=-1$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: $\\frac{x^{n+1}+y^{n+1}}{x^n+y^n}=\\sqrt{x y} \\Rightarrow x^{n+1}+y^{n+1}=\\sqrt{x y}\\left(x^n+y^n\\right)$\n$$\n\\mathrm{x}^{\\mathrm{n}+\\frac{1}{2}}\\left(\\mathrm{x}^{\\frac{1}{2}}-\\mathrm{y}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)=\\mathrm{y}^{\\mathrm{n}+\\frac{1}{2}}\\left(\\mathrm{x}^{\\frac{1}{2}}-\\mathrm{y}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right),\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{x}}{\\mathrm{y}}\\right)^{\\mathrm{n}+\\frac{1}{2}}=1 \\quad \\mathrm{n}=-\\frac{1}{2}\n$$"
  }
}